# Git & Environments

## The three main branches
| Branch | Where it exists | Environment | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `develop` | **Local + GitHub** — the **only** main branch on the developer machine | Railway `development` | Integration of all work |
| `staging` | **GitHub only** | Railway `staging` | Production-like testing (same config/infra shape as prod, separate data). **Not** production |
| `main` | **GitHub only** | Railway `production` | Real users. **Must work with zero known bugs** |

- Locally you work on `develop` and on short-lived work branches created **from** `develop`.
  Never check out, create or track `staging`/`main` locally (`git fetch` to inspect remote refs is fine).
- Work branches sit **before** `develop`: `feature/<ticket>-<slug>`, `fix/<ticket>-<slug>`,
  `chore/<slug>`, `docs/<slug>` → PR into `develop`.
- `hotfix/<slug>` is the only exception: created on GitHub from `main`; its pushes run the full pipeline on the
  **staging** environment; then PR into `main`, and back-merge `main → staging → develop` the same day.

## Promotion order — always ascending, never skip
`work branch → develop → staging → main`
- PRs into `staging` come only from `develop`; PRs into `main` come only from `staging` (or `hotfix/*`).
  CI enforces this (`promotion-guard`).
- `main` never contains a commit that isn't in `staging`; `staging` never one that isn't in `develop`.
- Updating Railway happens **only** by merging on GitHub — GitHub triggers Railway. Never deploy around Git.

## Test levels per branch
| Stage | Level | What runs |
|---|---|---|
| PR: work branch → `develop` | **Partial** | lint, typecheck, unit, build, secret scan, dependency audit |
| `develop` (after merge) and PR `develop → staging` | **Full** | everything in partial + integration, contract, E2E, accessibility, performance/Lighthouse, security (SAST/DAST), load smoke, visual regression |
| PR `staging → main` | **Full + release** | full suite on staging + load test + UAT sign-off + security review |
| After prod deploy | Smoke | read-only health and critical-path checks |
Details in `06-testing-quality`.

## Merge blocking
- Branch protection on `develop`, `staging`, `main`: required status checks must be **green** — no merge
  while any check is red or pending. No direct pushes. Enforced for admins on `staging` and `main`.
- Conversations must be resolved before merge.

## Commits — Conventional Commits
`<type>(<scope>): <summary>` — `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`,
`revert`; `!` / `BREAKING CHANGE:` for breaking changes. English, imperative, ≤ 72 chars.

## Pull requests
- Use the PR template, link the issue, explain *why*. Include test evidence, screenshots, migrations,
  env changes and a rollback plan. Prefer < 400 changed lines.
- Squash-merge work branches into `develop`; merge commits for promotions. Tag `vX.Y.Z` on every merge to `main`.

## Environments
- Each environment has its own database, Redis, secrets, Meta app / WhatsApp test number, payment sandbox,
  analytics property (or filtered view), and domain (`dev.`, `staging.`, apex).
- `development` and `staging` are `noindex` and protected; pixels/analytics in test mode.
- Production data never copied down unless anonymized.
